{"id":"st2003","designation":"ST 2003","title":"Types Dictionary Structure","state":"active","suite":null,"official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st2003/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st2003/","checked_at":"2026-11-11"},"scope":"This standard defines the structure of a dictionary of types for all registers defined by SMPTE ST 336. These types may be used in a range of applications such as production workflow applications, data exchange formats, and archival asset management systems. The standard normatively defines universal identifiers, type names, definitions, and standardized symbols, as well as other normative and informative fields. Applications of individual entries will vary, but, when used, shall conform to the definitions and formats in the types dictionary.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"Conformance Notation","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"3 Normative References","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"4 Types Dictionary Structure","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"4.1 Compatibility with Other Data Structures","page":5},{"level":2,"title":"Individual Classes of Types","page":5},{"level":3,"title":"Class 1: Basic Types","page":6},{"level":3,"title":"4.2.2 Class 2: Enumerated Types","page":7},{"level":3,"title":"4.2.3 Class 3: Record Types","page":7},{"level":3,"title":"4.2.4 Class 4: Multiples","page":7},{"level":3,"title":"4.2.5 Class 5: Reference Types","page":10},{"level":3,"title":"4.2.6 Class 6: Choice Types","page":10},{"level":3,"title":"4.2.7 Class 8: Controlled Vocabularies","page":11},{"level":3,"title":"4.2.8 Class 13: Organizationally registered for public use","page":11},{"level":3,"title":"4.2.9 Class 14: Organizationally registered as private","page":12},{"level":3,"title":"4.2.10 Class 15: Experimental","page":12},{"level":2,"title":"4.3 Derivation of Types (Informative)","page":12},{"level":2,"title":"4.4 Dictionary Structure and Format","page":13},{"level":3,"title":"4.4.1 Register","page"